{"name":"Longhorn","hex":"#d88e5f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"longhorn","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A breed of beef cattle, having long horns, bred in Texas and other parts of southwest United States.","Ellipsis of longhorn beetle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/longhorn"}],"entries":[{"title":"English Longhorn","blocks":[{"text":"The Longhorn or British Longhorn is a British breed of beef cattle characterised by long curving horns. It originated in northern England, in the counties of Lancashire, Westmorland and Yorkshire, and later spread to the English Midlands and to Ireland. It was originally a slow heavy draught animal; cows gave a little milk, although high in fat. In the eighteenth century Robert Bakewell applied his methods of selective breeding to these cattle, which for a short time became the predominant British breed. Both the numbers and the quality of the breed declined throughout the nineteenth century and for much of the twentieth. A breed society was formed in 1878, and a herd-book published in that year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/English_Longhorn_cow_and_calf.jpg/330px-English_Longhorn_cow_and_calf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_Longhorn","wikidata":"Q3259108"},{"title":"Texas Longhorn","blocks":[{"text":"The Texas Longhorn is an American breed of beef cattle, characterized by its long horns, which can span more than 8 ft (2.4 m) from tip to tip. It derives from cattle brought from the Iberian Peninsula to the Americas by Spanish conquistadors from the time of the Second Voyage of Christopher Columbus until about 1512. For hundreds of years the cattle lived a semi-feral existence on the rangelands; they have a higher tolerance of heat and drought than most European breeds. The coat can be of any color or mix of colors; in some 40% of the cattle it is some shade of red, often a light red."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Texas_Longhorn_cow.jpg/330px-Texas_Longhorn_cow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas_Longhorn","wikidata":"Q390214"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/English_Longhorn_bull%2C_Quenby.jpg/500px-English_Longhorn_bull%2C_Quenby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/English_Longhorn_bull%2C_Quenby.jpg/500px-English_Longhorn_bull%2C_Quenby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bull at Quenby Hall, Leicestershire","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEnglish_Longhorn_bull%2C_Quenby.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Longhorn_cows%2C_Cherry_Lodge_Farm_-_geograph.org.uk_-_797591.jpg/500px-Longhorn_cows%2C_Cherry_Lodge_Farm_-_geograph.org.uk_-_797591.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Longhorn_cows%2C_Cherry_Lodge_Farm_-_geograph.org.uk_-_797591.jpg/500px-Longhorn_cows%2C_Cherry_Lodge_Farm_-_geograph.org.uk_-_797591.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"On Parsonage Down, in Wiltshire","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALonghorn_cows%2C_Cherry_Lodge_Farm_-_geograph.org.uk_-_797591.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Texas_Longhorn_Steer_Rocksprings.jpg/500px-Texas_Longhorn_Steer_Rocksprings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Texas_Longhorn_Steer_Rocksprings.jpg/1280px-Texas_Longhorn_Steer_Rocksprings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thu